        "# 🧬 Project 1 Assessment: Identifying Mutations in NGS Data\n",
        "\n",
        "This task simulates part of a **next-generation sequencing (NGS) data analysis workflow**, in which sequencing reads are compared with a known **reference sequence** to identify nucleotide differences, or **mismatches**. These mismatches can then be used to identify and characterise mutations within the sequenced DNA.\n",
        "\n",
        "You have been provided with sequencing data from **six samples** of fission yeast (*S. pombe*), a widely used model organism in genomics research:\n",
        "- The first three samples (`sample1`, `sample2`, and `sample3`) were treated with a **genotoxic agent**\n",
        "- The other three samples (`sample4`, `sample5`, and `sample6`) were untreated controls.\n",
        "\n",
        "Within each sample, 1,000 sequencing reads were made — some reads perfectly match the reference sequence, while others contain one or more **nucleotide mismatches**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Your goal is to develop a Python program that identifies and characterises these mismatches, allowing you to investigate how mutation patterns differ between the treated and untreated samples."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "WPzS1Wj55cbx"
      }
    },
