        "## Step 1 — Validate each read and record any errors\n",
        "## Function: `validate_read(sequence, reference)`\n",
        "\n",
        "### 👍 You can assume:\n",
        "- `reference` is a non-empty string containing only uppercase A/C/G/T.\n",
        "- `sequence` is a string, but nothing about its length or contents.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🎯 Aims:\n",
        "- Check that an individual read is the same length as the reference and contains only valid characters (A/C/G/T)\n",
        "- \"Repair\" any reads that contain valid lower-case characters -> upper-case\n",
        "- Return a dictionary with the following keys:\n",
        "\n",
        "    - `sequence`: the upper-case version of the sequence input, including when invalid.\n",
        "    - `valid`: `True` only when the length matches the reference and every character is A/C/G/T.\n",
        "    - `errors`: a list of strings. Include `\"wrong_length\"` first if lengths differ, then `\"invalid_characters\"` if any character is outside A/C/G/T. Include both when both apply. A valid read has `[]`.\n",
